There is more than one artist with this name, including: 
1) Actress is the artist alias of British electronic musician Darren Cunningham from Wolverhampton; 
2) Actress was a German chaos/noise rock band from Wiesbaden; 
3) Actress was a project of American musician Kaleb Saldate; 
4) Actress was an American rock band featuring Arthur "Killer" Kane (bass), Rick Rivets (guitar) and Billy Murcia (drums); 
5) Actress was American duo of brothers Aaron and Josh Ficchi from Hollywood, CA.

There are several artists with the name Elder;

1) Elder is a four-piece  progressive rock band from Boston, Massachusetts consisting of frontman Nick DiSalvo, bassist Jack Donovan, guitarist/keyboardist Michael Risberg and drummer Georg Edert. They have released seven full-length albums since 2006 and multiple demos and EPs.

Elder is a genre-pushing rock band that melds heavy psychedelic sounds with progressive elements and evocative soundscapes.

There are at least two artists sharing the name Magic Lantern;

1) Magic Lantern is a psychedelic / space rock band from Long Beach, California, USA who play droney, long-form music in the vein of bands like Amon Düül II, Hawkwind, and Loop.  They have self-released the cassette, titled "At the Mountains of Madness", their other releases are highly limited and mostly sold out. In 2008 they released the highly acclaimed "High Beams" on LP.

In 2010 the band released the LP/CD "Platoon" and the 7" "Showstopper/Cypress", both on Not Not Fun.
